import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Synthgarage Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy for Synthgarage, the universal preset librarian for Mac, iPhone, and iPad."
>
  <section class="hero hero-compact">
    <h1>Synthgarage Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="platforms">Effective Date: 11 September 2026</p>
    <p class="platforms">Developer: Bucket Brigade (New Zealand)</p>
    <p class="lead">
      Synthgarage is a synthesiser patch librarian. It keeps your sound library on your own
      devices. Bucket Brigade operates no servers and holds no copy of your sound library.
    </p>
    <p>
      There is no Synthgarage account, no advertising, and no tracking across apps or websites.
      Nothing is sold or shared with data brokers. Where your library leaves your device, it goes
      to a service <strong>you</strong> signed into — Apple’s iCloud, or a cloud storage account
      you connect yourself — under your own agreement with that provider.
    </p>
    <p>
      The one thing the app sends on its own behalf is anonymised telemetry, so we can tell which
      features are used and where the app fails. It is not linked to your identity, and it can be
      turned off.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      Synthgarage is published by Bucket Brigade, New Zealand. For privacy questions, contact
      support@synthgarage.com.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What the app handles, and where it goes</h2>

    <h3>Your patch library — on your device</h3>
    <p>
      Imported SysEx files, the sounds decoded from them, names, tags, collections, and the file
      and folder names they came from. Stored locally on the device.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you are signed into iCloud and have iCloud Drive enabled, this library is mirrored through
      Apple CloudKit to your own private iCloud database, so it appears on your other devices. That
      database belongs to your Apple Account. Bucket Brigade cannot read it, and has no
      administrative access to it.
    </p>

    <h3>Instrument and MIDI settings — on your device</h3>
    <p>
      The names of MIDI ports and interfaces you select, MIDI channels, and per-instrument
      connection settings. These are stored on the device only and are not mirrored, because a port
      name on one machine means nothing on another.
    </p>

    <h3>App preferences and diagnostics — on your device</h3>
    <p>
      Interface state, import options, and a diagnostic log used for troubleshooting. The log stays
      on the device and is shown only inside the app. It is not transmitted anywhere.
    </p>

    <h3>Purchases</h3>
    <p>
      Additional synthesiser support is sold as one-time in-app purchases. Purchases are processed
      by Apple, and payment details never reach the app or Bucket Brigade. The app receives from
      Apple’s StoreKit only the fact that a purchase is valid, and records which items are
      unlocked.
    </p>
    <p>
      Apple’s handling of your purchase is governed by
      <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/">Apple’s privacy policy</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Optional cloud backup — to an account you connect</h2>
    <p>
      You may connect a cloud storage account so that Synthgarage keeps a plain copy of your sounds
      there. This is <strong>off unless you turn it on</strong>.
    </p>
    <p>When enabled, the app copies to the folder it creates in your account:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>SysEx files you import, byte-for-byte as they arrived, and their original filenames</li>
      <li>sounds created in the app, and dumps received from an instrument, as .syx files</li>
      <li>folders named after the manufacturer and model the sounds are for</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Supported services and the access requested</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>iCloud Drive</strong> — the app’s own container: a folder belonging to this app</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Dropbox</strong> — files.content.write, app-folder scoped: write only, inside
        Apps/SynthGarage
      </li>
      <li><strong>Google Drive</strong> — drive.file: only files and folders this app creates</li>
      <li><strong>OneDrive</strong> — Files.ReadWrite.AppFolder: only the app’s own folder</li>
      <li><strong>Any other folder</strong> — a folder you choose: that folder only</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Two things follow, and both are deliberate:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>The permissions requested are the narrowest each service offers.</strong>
        Synthgarage cannot read the rest of your Dropbox, Drive or OneDrive, and does not ask to.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>The files go from your device to your account.</strong> They do not pass through
        Bucket Brigade, and we never hold a copy.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Sign-in uses OAuth. The resulting access token is stored in your device’s Keychain, is not
      included in device backups shared with us, and is deliberately not synchronised between your
      devices. Disconnecting in Settings ▸ Backup deletes it from the device; revoking access at
      the provider ends it entirely.
    </p>
    <p>
      Your use of those services is governed by their own policies:
      <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/">Apple</a> ·
      <a href="https://www.dropbox.com/privacy">Dropbox</a> ·
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google</a> ·
      <a href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement">Microsoft</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Anonymised telemetry</h2>
    <p>
      Synthgarage sends anonymised telemetry through TelemetryDeck, a privacy-focused analytics
      service, so we can see which features are used and where the app fails. It is not linked to
      your identity: TelemetryDeck receives no persistent device identifier, signals are not used
      to build a profile, are not combined with data from other sources, and are never used for
      advertising.
    </p>
    <p>
      Telemetry carries usage and diagnostic information, not your content. It can be turned off in
      the app’s settings, which stops any further signals immediately.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What the app does not do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>No advertising, and no advertising identifiers.</li>
      <li>
        No tracking across apps or websites, and no data shared with anyone for tracking. The
        telemetry above is <strong>not</strong> tracking as the App Store defines it: it is not
        linked to your identity and is not combined with data from other companies.
      </li>
      <li>No Synthgarage account, and no personal details collected to use the app.</li>
      <li>No sale or sharing of personal information.</li>
      <li>No attribution SDKs, no advertising SDKs, and no third-party crash reporter.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>No copy of your library reaches Bucket Brigade.</strong> Your library lives on your
        device, in your own iCloud, and in any cloud storage account you connect.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Only two pieces of third-party code in the app communicate over a network: the Dropbox SDK,
      used solely to sign in to and write to the account you connect, and TelemetryDeck, used
      solely for the anonymised telemetry described above.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Legal basis for processing</h2>
    <p>
      For users in the UK and EU: your library is held on your own device, in your own iCloud, and
      in cloud storage accounts you connect, so Bucket Brigade does not process it at all. For the
      limited processing that remains, our bases are performance of a contract — validating and
      restoring in-app purchases, which Apple carries out — and legitimate interests in
      understanding and improving the app, for anonymised telemetry, which you can switch off at
      any time.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      Synthgarage is not directed at children and does not knowingly collect information from them.
      It is intended for users aged 16 and over, and we do not knowingly collect personal
      information from anyone under that age. If you believe a child has provided us with personal
      information, contact support@synthgarage.com and we will delete it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Security</h2>
    <p>
      Patch data is stored using the operating system’s own protections, including file-level
      encryption on a locked device. Cloud storage access tokens are held in the Keychain. The
      catalogue of synthesiser definitions shipped with the app is stored encrypted. No system is
      perfectly secure, and data held in your own iCloud or cloud storage account is protected by
      that provider and by the strength of your own account security.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Retention and deletion</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>On your device:</strong> deleting the app removes its local data. Individual
        sounds, synthesisers and collections can be deleted in the app at any time.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>In your iCloud:</strong> managed through your Apple Account, in Settings ▸ Apple
        Account ▸ iCloud.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>In connected cloud storage:</strong> the folder is yours. Delete it, or revoke the
        app’s access, in that provider’s own settings. Disconnecting in the app stops further
        copies being written but does not delete what is already there — that is your copy to keep
        or remove.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Telemetry:</strong> anonymised, so individual signals cannot be traced back to you
        and located for deletion. Turning it off stops any further signals immediately.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct, delete, port or restrict
      the processing of your personal information, and to object to it, under the New Zealand
      Privacy Act 2020, the UK and EU GDPR, and comparable laws including the California Consumer
      Privacy Act where they apply to you.
    </p>
    <p>
      Because Bucket Brigade holds no library of your data, most such requests are satisfied
      directly: the data is on your device and in accounts you control. Telemetry is anonymised and
      cannot be linked back to you, so there is no record of yours within it to access, correct or
      export. For anything you have sent us directly, such as an email, contact
      support@synthgarage.com and we will respond within 20 working days.
    </p>
    <p>
      You may also complain to the New Zealand Office of the Privacy Commissioner
      (<a href="https://www.privacy.org.nz">privacy.org.nz</a>), or, if you are in the UK or EU, to
      your local data protection authority.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>International transfers</h2>
    <p>
      Bucket Brigade is based in New Zealand. Because we hold no copy of your library, transfers of
      your data happen between you and the services you choose — Apple, Dropbox, Google, Microsoft
      — under those providers’ own terms and safeguards, rather than to us. Anonymised telemetry is
      processed by TelemetryDeck on our behalf and carries no information that identifies you.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy changes materially, the updated version will be posted at
      https://www.synthgarage.com/synthgarage-privacy with a new effective date, and where the
      change requires it you will be told in the app.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Bucket Brigade</p>
    <p>Publisher, Synthgarage</p>
    <p>Email: support@synthgarage.com</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
